{"id":231279721268977,"type":"artist","name":"Super Furry Animals","artist":null,"year":1993,"weight":15,"info":{"tags":["indie","indie rock","britpop","alternative","rock"],"country":"GB","begin":"1993","kind":"Group","similar":["Gruff Rhys","Gorky's Zygotic Mynci","Supergrass","The Bluetones","The Charlatans","Catatonia","The Beta Band","Longpigs","Manic Street Preachers","Shed Seven"],"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Super_Furry_Animals_live_in_Barcelona_2007.jpg?width=500","bio":"Formados en Cardiff, Gales, en 1993, Super Furry Animals empezaron haciendo música electrónica aunque pronto incorporaron destellos de psicodelia y de rock progresivo a sus canciones. \n\nEn un primer momento, despuntaron con el punk progresivo de su fabuloso debut \"Fuzzy Logic\" (1996) y con el art-rock enfadado de \"Guerrilla\" (1999). En ambos álbumes ya se dejaron influenciar por esos ramalazos electrónicos que han marcado su brillante carrera, con los que demuestran que combinan como nadie su amor por The Beach Boys y su fervor por Orbital."},"works":[{"id":192702477776715,"type":"album","name":"Fuzzy Logic","artist":"Super Furry Animals","year":1996,"weight":16,"yt":"Sol7-jZNdmQ","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":238350566072075,"name":"Pitchfork: The 50 Best Britpop Albums","rank":27,"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","rank":808,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":100380232078870,"type":"album","name":"Radiator","artist":"Super Furry Animals","year":1997,"weight":12,"yt":"ydl8CwwdPDo","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":238350566072075,"name":"Pitchfork: The 50 Best Britpop Albums","rank":39,"scaruffi":null},{"id":14239102054361,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 1997","rank":127,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":125086826174918,"type":"so